course: dictionary
lesson: 12574
title: Making things smaller
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diminished means made smaller, fewer or weaker. It is the past form of the verb diminish, so you can also say a supply diminishes, or is diminishing, as it gets smaller. «The sun's light was diminished by the thick clouds.» The clouds made the light weaker, so less of it got through.
explain: Look for the clues. The words around diminished tell you what got smaller. «Our water supply has greatly diminished during the dry summer.» Greatly is a clue: the water did not shrink a little, it shrank a lot.
explain: In maths, diminished by means minus. «Twenty diminished by five» means 20 take away 5, so the answer is 15. In a story, diminished can show someone losing strength or respect. «Her confidence diminished after the harsh words» means she felt less sure of herself.
fact: Diminished means made smaller, fewer or weaker.
fact: «Diminished by» means «made smaller by», or minus in maths: 20 diminished by 5 is 15.
fact: Diminish is the verb: things diminish, diminishes, diminished and diminishing.
fact: In formal writing, to be diminished means to become less important or less respected.
fact: In music, a diminished chord is a little smaller than the usual one.
exercise: «The sun's light was diminished by the thick clouds.» What does diminished mean here? | Moved to a different place | *Made weaker, so less light got through | Turned into a shadow | Made brighter and warmer
exercise: What is 20 diminished by 5? | 25 | 100 | *15 | 5
exercise: «Our water supply has greatly diminished during the dry summer.» What does this suggest? | *The water became much smaller in amount | The water was cleaned and made safe | The water became much bigger | The water was poured into the lake
test: «Her confidence diminished after the harsh words.» What does this show? | Her confidence grew bigger | She forgot her name | Her confidence was painted red | *Her confidence became weaker
test: In music, what is a diminished chord? | A chord played as loudly as possible | *A chord that is a little smaller than the usual one | A chord played only by a choir | A chord with extra notes added
exam: Which phrase means «made smaller by» in a maths sum? | As bright as ever by | *Diminished by | Brightly lit by | Greatly enlarged by
